.Dd November 14, 2026
.Dt NEWFS_EXFAT 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm newfs_exfat
.Nd construct a new exFAT file system
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl Nv
.Op Fl C Ar create-size
.Op Fl c Ar cluster-size
.Op Fl I Ar volume-id
.Op Fl L Ar label
.Op Fl p Ar partition-offset
.Op Fl S Ar sector-size
.Op Fl s Ar size
.Ar special
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility initializes an exFAT
file system on the device or image file specified by
.Ar special .
.Pp
The layout created follows the official exFAT specification:
.Bl -bullet
.It
Main Volume Boot Record (VBR) consisting of sectors 0 through 11, including
the primary boot sector, extended boot sectors, OEM parameter sector, and
a 32-bit checksum sector covering the entire boot sequence.
.It
Backup Volume Boot Record consisting of sectors 12 through 23 duplicating the
Main VBR.
.It
File Allocation Table (FAT) mapping cluster connectivity, located at a sector
offset of at least 24 per section 3.1.6 of the exFAT specification.
.It
Cluster heap aligned to the cluster boundary per section 3.1.8 of the exFAT
specification, containing initial system files: Allocation Bitmap (type 0x81),
standard compressed Unicode Up-Case Table (type 0x82), and the Root
Directory containing the Volume Label (type 0x83) and system pointers.
.El
.Pp
Volumes must be at least 1 MiB in size per section 3.1.5 of the exFAT
specification.
The cluster count is bounded between 1 and 4,294,967,285
.Pq 2^32 - 11
per section 3.1.9 of the exFAT specification.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl C Ar create-size
Create a new file of the specified size before initializing the file system.
The size may include suffix units such as
.Ql k ,
.Ql m ,
.Ql g ,
or
.Ql t .
The create size must be at least 1 MiB.
.It Fl c Ar cluster-size
Specify the cluster size in bytes, or if 128 or less, the number of sectors
per cluster.
The size may include suffix units such as
.Ql k
or
.Ql m .
If not specified, a default cluster size is chosen according to volume size:
4 KiB for volumes smaller than 256 MiB, 32 KiB for volumes up to 32 GiB,
and for larger volumes, 128 KiB capped at the system buffer cache maximum
.Pq Va vfs.maxbcachebuf , typically 64 KiB
to ensure compatibility with the
.Fx
kernel.
If an explicit cluster size exceeding
.Va vfs.maxbcachebuf
is specified, a warning is issued that the volume will fail to mount on
standard
.Fx
systems.
The maximum cluster count supported by the exFAT specification is
4,294,967,285
.Pq 2^32 - 11 .
FAT tables are formatted in streaming chunks, bounding memory usage during
initialization regardless of volume size.
.It Fl I Ar volume-id
Specify the 32-bit volume serial number in decimal or hexadecimal.
If omitted, a random serial number is generated.
.It Fl L Ar label
Specify the volume label, up to 11 characters in length.
The label is stored in UTF-16LE in the root directory.
Per section 7.2.3 of the exFAT specification, the label must not contain
characters in the range 0x0000 through 0x001F or any of the characters:
.Ql \&" ,
.Ql * ,
.Ql / ,
.Ql : ,
.Ql < ,
.Ql > ,
.Ql \&? ,
.Ql \e ,
or
.Ql | .
.It Fl N
Do not create or write to the file system.
Calculates and displays the computed geometry and layout parameters.
.It Fl p Ar partition-offset
Specify the volume-relative sector offset of the partition containing
the exFAT volume.
The default is 0.
.It Fl S Ar sector-size
Bytes per logical sector.
Accepted values are 512, 1024, 2048, or 4096 bytes.
When formatting a disk device, the sector size is automatically detected
from the underlying device if not explicitly specified.
Default is 512 bytes for file images.
.It Fl s Ar size
Specify the file system size in bytes or sectors.
.It Fl v
Verbose mode.
Displays detailed sizing and cluster offsets.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Create a 64 MiB exFAT image file with volume label
.Dq FLASHDRIVE :
.Pp
.Dl "# newfs_exfat -C 64M -L FLASHDRIVE /tmp/flash.img"
.Pp
Format a partition with 32 KiB clusters and display calculated parameters:
.Pp
.Dl "# newfs_exfat -v -c 32k -L USBDRV /dev/da0s1"
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr exfat 4 ,
.Xr fsck_exfat 8 ,
.Xr glabel 8 ,
.Xr mount_exfat 8 ,
.Xr newfs_msdos 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
utility first appeared in
.Fx 15.1 .
.Sh AUTHORS
The
.Nm
utility was developed for the
.Fx
Project.
